From ecedde596e4746d6d726f29d1e95f6e90b9edd69 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: marie-222 <289302950+marie-222@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 09:39:56 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] desktop-shell: ignore a window move for a surface that has no
 shell surface

shell_backend_request_window_move() looked up the shell surface of the
surface, tolerated NULL in the is_localmove_pending check, and then
dereferenced it unconditionally in
assert(!shsurf->snapped.is_maximized_requested).

msrdc also sends WindowMove for windows that are not top level windows
(for example a 16x16 window at (0,0) that has no app id). Such a surface has
a view but no shell surface, so Weston died with a NULL dereference
(SIGSEGV at address 0x141, the offset of snapped.is_maximized_requested in
struct shell_surface) as soon as one of them was reported.

Return when there is no shell surface, as
shell_backend_request_window_{minimize,maximize,restore,snap}() already do.
A surface without a shell surface is not a window that a move can be
requested for, so nothing is lost; the dead "shsurf &&" test is removed.
---
 desktop-shell/shell.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/desktop-shell/shell.c b/desktop-shell/shell.c
index 5e00ca4e..97f0d4d0 100644
--- a/desktop-shell/shell.c
+++ b/desktop-shell/shell.c
@@ -6132,10 +6132,10 @@ shell_backend_request_window_move(struct weston_surface *surface, int x, int y,
 	struct weston_coord_global pos;
 
 	view = get_default_view(surface);
-	if (!view)
+	if (!view || !shsurf)
 		return;
 
-	if (shsurf && shsurf->shell->is_localmove_pending) {
+	if (shsurf->shell->is_localmove_pending) {
 		shsurf->shell->is_localmove_pending = false;
 	}
 
-- 
